  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a logged-in member reading a topic, I want to write and send a reply, so that I can take part in the discussion from the app.\n\n### Scope\n\nReply sheet opened from the reader's 'Répondre': text editor, send through LOT-048 as the **selected** account (Q-8), success only when HFR confirmed it, then the reader reloads at the new post's anchor. Draft autosaved per context (LOT-063) and restored; dismissing asks keep/discard. Non-BMP characters refused before sending with a clear message (Q-3).\n\n- Module: App · Difficulty: medium · Priority: high · MVP\n- Implements: legacy parity (no FEAT)\n- Absorbs: MVP (#166, operator 2026-10-27): the posting-basics screen over 036, 037, 048. User feedback: composer glitches (p. 498-506), drafts safe\n- Legacy sources (read-only, `origin/master`): `AnswerView.swift` (`AnswerView`, `ReplyDraftStore`, `ComposerDraftPersistence`), `ReplyService.swift` (`ForumReplyPostingService`); legacy backlog HFR-001 (third-party keyboards)\n- Spec: `docs/lots/LOT-084-*.md`\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-048 (#74, in-progress)\n- LOT-063 (#88, done)\n- LOT-081 (#99, in-progress)\n- LOT-083 (#101, in-progress)\n\n### Blocked by\n\ndependencies not done: LOT-048 (#74, in-progress), LOT-081 (#99, in-progress), LOT-083 (#101, in-progress)\n\n### Model\n\nOpus → Fable (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- #131\n- #130\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Success shown only on LOT-048's confirmed success; any other outcome keeps the text and shows an actionable French message.\n- [ ] Draft saved while typing (debounced, normal code path, LESSONS 48) and restored after a kill; cleared only after a confirmed send.\n- [ ] Third-party keyboards allowed (no `asciiCapable`, legacy HFR-001); text never hidden by the keyboard.\n- [ ] Locked topic / not allowed to post: the composer is not offered, or shows HFR's reason (per #131 once captured).\n- [ ] View logic lives in `@Observable @MainActor` models tested with Swift Testing in `App/SwiftHFRTests/`; each new test is shown to fail without the change.\n- [ ] `xcodebuild build test` green on the iPhone 18 Pro and an iPad simulator (iOS 27.0), and the `App build + tests` CI job green.\n- [ ] UI strings in French; light, dark and Dynamic Type XL checked; no new dependency; no HFR fact without a source (legacy file:line or fixture).\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).",
